is a fairly common pattern when building containers on top of other containers, and is similar to (but not quite) the Decorator pattern.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To use the global sleep function, you need to import the library which defines it - Foundation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import Foundation and build a function called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run()"},{"type":"text","text":" that will print our Reminders to the terminal after the duration has passed for that reminder."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because we are not yet building this async, our Reminders will print out sequentially, with each one’s duration ticking after the next."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"code":"2-1-4.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Currently this loses data due to casting from Double to UInt32 (it will floor any decimal values). This is OK for now, as future steps will fix this issue."}]}],"title":"Building a ReminderManager","anchor":"Building-a-ReminderManager","contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Build a ReminderManager that keeps track of all active Reminders and prints them when necessary.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}]},{"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By using an instance of "},{"code":"ReminderManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", we can keep track of our reminders and print them out as needed.","type":"text"}]}]}],"anchor":"Building-and-Delivering-Reminders-In-mainswift","title":"Building and Delivering Reminders In main.swift","stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In main.swift, declare an instance of our "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ReminderManager"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"2-2-1.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create an array of reminders for us to print out."}]}],"media":null,"code":"2-2-2.swift","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In a real-world application you would be receiving these from a file, the network, or user input. For now, we are doing what’s called “mocking” the data for testing purposes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You could also define an initiliazer for ","type":"text"},{"code":"ReminderManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and pass an array of reminders to that instead, but we want our interface to be able to add new reminders at later times.","type":"text"}]}],"code":"2-2-3.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterate through the list of reminders and add them to the manager.","type":"text"}]}],"media":null,"type":"step"},{"type":"step","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You should see something similar to the preview in your terminal.","type":"text"}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call the run function on the manager.","type":"text"}]}],"code":"2-2-4.swift","runtimePreview":"2-2-4-image.png","media":null}]}]},{"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","action":{"overridingTitle":"Get started","isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Documentation\/tutorials\/Documentation\/4-Concurrency","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}]},"kind":"callToAction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Modify your executable application to work well with Swift Concurrency."}],"title":"Swift Concurrency"}],"hierarchy":{"modules":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/Documentation\/tutorials\/0-TOC\/What's-in-a-Reminder-"